From: zhangjianguo <janegle@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: airoha: recalibrate JCPLL VCO on every USXGMII link-up

The host-side lane fails to re-lock after copper re-AN events: the
link comes up for ~1 s and then drops, and the in-driver recovery
loop only re-runs pcs_config (which performs the JCPLL recal) about
91 s later. Recalibrating the JCPLL VCO in the pcs link-up callback
makes the lane re-lock immediately on every USXGMII link-up.

Signed-off-by: zhangjianguo <janegle@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c
@@ -998,6 +998,15 @@
 	maps = &priv->maps[port->index];
 	data = priv->data;
 
+	/* Prevention: the host-side lane fails to re-lock after copper
+	 * re-AN events (link comes up for ~1 s then drops) and the
+	 * recovery loop only re-runs pcs_config ~91 s later. Recalibrate
+	 * the JCPLL VCO on every USXGMII link-up so the lane re-locks
+	 * immediately instead.
+	 */
+	if (interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_USXGMII)
+		an7581_pcs_jcpll_recal(priv, port->index, interface);
+
 	if (neg_mode == PHYLINK_PCS_NEG_INBAND_ENABLED &&
 	    interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_SGMII) {
 		regmap_update_bits(maps->hsgmii_rate_adp,
